---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site title="About">
  <section class="wrap page-intro narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">PLAY · INVESTIGATE · MAKE</p>
    <h1>
      Computing you
      <br />
      can get hold of.
    </h1>
    <p class="intro">
      KajLights explores computing logic, hardware protocols and connected
      systems through play and creativity.
    </p>
    <p>
      LightVM makes a small light controller programmable. kaj-fi explores
      derived audio features while keeping raw sound on the device. The website
      brings learning and device maintenance together; the implementation
      projects build their own firmware.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section narrow prose">
    <h2>Experimental, and honest about it</h2>
    <p>
      These are experimental projects. Available features, installation methods
      and validation evidence are shown explicitly. A source commit or CI build
      is not presented as a public firmware release.
    </p>
    <h2>Your browser, your devices</h2>
    <p>
      Device connections run directly in your browser. No KajLights account or
      cloud device database is required. Remembered labels stay in this browser;
      nicknames you explicitly save are written to the device. Firmware assets
      come from the website’s verified release mirror.
    </p>
    <h2>Help make the workshop</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, experiments and contributions belong alongside the source.
      User-facing learning material and maintenance tools belong here;
      implementation details remain with their projects.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/KajLights">
      Explore the source ↗
    </a>
  </section>
</Site>
